    "Model exhibits severe upward drift bias when recent history shows a downtrend followed by a spike; true outcomes often reverse immediately (e.g., Example 5 Day 1 vs Model Day 1).",
    "Sentiment spikes (0.25-0.33) in the last 3 days of history correlate with immediate model overreaction to prior lows, causing significant overshoots in the first 7 forecast days.",
    "Model fails to capture mean reversion volatility; it assumes linear continuation after a crash while true outcomes show sharp V-shapes or continued declines depending on sentiment decay.",
    "Forecast horizon error: Model predicts steady growth over 30 days, but true outcomes are highly volatile with high-frequency swings that invalidate the linear projection assumption.",
    "When sentiment history shows low values (0.00) during a price drop, the model underestimates the depth of the subsequent recovery spike seen in Day 19-24 of the forecast window."
